# How values compare (see docs/reference/builtins.md#equatable-comparable-and-hashable).

## How a value compares with another, which compare gives (see Comparable).
export enum Ordering
  LESS
  EQUAL
  GREATER

## The types that have `equals`: every type that `==` compares, by its own equals or compare, or
## as `==` does.
export interface Equatable
  equals: (Self) -> Bool

## The types that have `compare`, which gives their `<` and the like: the numbers, String, and the
## classes and structs that have their own, which gives their `==` too.
export interface Comparable
  compare: (Self) -> Ordering

## The types that can be map keys and set items: equal values hash alike.
export interface Hashable
  equals: (Self) -> Bool
  hash: () -> Int

## The lesser of the values, the first if they are equal, by their compare (see Comparable).
# Of two alone, as a third would make an array at each call; an Iterable's min takes more.
export min := <T: Comparable>(a: T, b: T): T -> b < a then b else a

## The greater of the values, the first if they are equal.
export max := <T: Comparable>(a: T, b: T): T -> b > a then b else a
